# Sub-tick interpolation of the gem-glint stars (scripts/check_glint_subtick.sh).
#   <bk2> | <V> | gem=<x>,<y> rec=<addr> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>]
# V is the tick whose primitives the intermediate present at V+1 replays; V-2
# opens the interval that present covers. Each gem is named by its mask
# component's centroid in the canonical capture at V, and must be unoccluded
# over the interval: a partly covered star's visible centroid measures the
# depth test rather than the rebase. Each gem's rec= names the pool record
# whose traced outline centroid is judged (PSX px); the mask centroid is
# reported only, since a rotating star's mask centroid traces an arc.
#
# The camera swings 14-17 PSX px per tick here, which is what separates a
# producer that interpolates from one that holds its tick pose.
#
# The gem judged is record 8006DF38, a near star (eight quads, 24 traced outline
# corners, extent 4.14 -> 4.00 PSX px over the interval), the only glint
# component in view: its mask is 25 px at canon(1540) and 29 px at canon(1542),
# so one flipped pixel is 1/29 of the mask; a rim pixel at the star's ~4 px
# native radius moves the centroid ~0.14 px against the 0.5 bound. Before the
# extent fix (OPENPETE_GLINT_EXTENT=0) the alpha-0.5 centroid read 0.14 px, with
# the fix 0.08 px; identity 0.00 on both.
#
# The row judged record 8006DF08 at V=1518 until the extent fix: a far cross
# with 3.0 px arms whose 21-22 px mask moves ~0.1 px per flipped pixel. It read
# 0.43 px before the fix, most of it the tick's corner truncation that the
# replay translates (the alpha-0 carve-out of the glint rebase), and 0.54 after,
# the whole change one pixel of the mask; the outline's own centre moved 0.003
# PSX px. No near star shows at 1518. The nearer VBLs with a visible near star
# fail the bound on the build without the fix as well (1536 1.12 px, 1538 1.60,
# 1540 0.57), the star partly covered by the terrain it rises from, so 1542 is
# the nearest V whose reading measures the rebase rather than the depth test.
# Mask centroid at alpha 0.5, capture px: 0.08 with the replay rotating
# against the routine's sense, 0.74 with its sense (the 29 px mask of a star
# turning 4 table entries between two rasters, no translation change).
# Geometric centroid at alpha 0.5, PSX px: 0.076 before, 0.107 after (alpha 0
# 0.221 before, 0.183 after); identity 0.000.
sunrise-spring-camera-swing.bk2 | 1542 | gem=417.1,241.8 rec=8006DF38 tol=0.5 step=10
